<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matsumae Yoshihiro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1548">1548</a>–<a href="/years/1618">1618</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Matsumae Yoshihiro was a Japanese lord of the Kakizaki family, which controlled southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hokkaido">Hokkaido</a>, then called Ezo. Taking the family name Matsumae, he received a charter from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> in 1604 granting him the exclusive right to trade with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ainu">Ainu</a>, which became the basis of the Matsumae domain. The domain lived on this trade rather than on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>.</p></div>
